les."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Algorithms use this refinement to number the live vertices and edges with arrays while holes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exist, instead of hashing every vertex and edge they meet. The bounds are upper bounds only.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Positions are never reused, so a bound counts every position ever handed out, and nothing in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the library allocates by it. Position-keyed state goes through a paged map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"_PositionNumbers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), O(live elements + pages).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s laws:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containsVertex(atPosition: p)"},{"text":" is true exactly for the positions of live vertices, all in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexPositionBound"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexPosition(of:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex(atPosition:)"},{"text":" are inverses, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" lists the live vertices in increasing position. Likewise","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"containsEdge(atPosition:)"},{"text":" is true exactly for the positions in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":", all in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgePositionBound"},{"text":", which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" lists in increasing order.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"conten